### Bind ParseUUIDPipe to Route Parameter

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/docs.nestjs.com/blob/master/content/pipes.md

Validates that a string route parameter matches UUID format using an instance of ParseUUIDPipe.

```typescript
@@filename()
@Get(':uuid')
async findOne(@Param('uuid', new ParseUUIDPipe()) uuid: string) {
  return this.catsService.findOne(uuid);
}
@@switch
@Get(':uuid')
@Bind(Param('uuid', new ParseUUIDPipe()))
async findOne(uuid) {
  return this.catsService.findOne(uuid);
}
```

--------------------------------

### Binding pipes

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/docs.nestjs.com/blob/master/content/pipes.md

> info **Hint** By default, `ParseUUIDPipe` accepts a UUID of any version (versions 1 through 8, Nil, and Max UUIDs). To require a specific version, pass the `version` option (`'1'`, `'2'`, `'3'`, `'4'`, `'5'`, `'6'`, `'7'`, or `'8'`). Starting with NestJS v12.1.2, the `version` option also accepts these versions as numbers (for example, `7`), and `'all'` to accept any version, the same as leaving `version` out. The `UUIDVersion` type describes these values and is exported from `@nestjs/common`.

--------------------------------

### Generic response DTO via @ApiOkResponse({ schema }) with $ref

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/docs.nestjs.com/blob/master/content/openapi/operations.md

Shows that when the return type involves generics (Promise<PaginatedDto<CatDto>>), TypeScript erases generic parameters at runtime. The developer must use the `schema` property with getSchemaPath() and allOf to manually compose the OpenAPI schema, because the SwaggerModule cannot infer generic types from the runtime return type alone.

```typescript
export class PaginatedDto<TData> {
  @ApiProperty()
  total: number;

  @ApiProperty()
  limit: number;

  @ApiProperty()
  offset: number;

  results: TData[];
}

export class CatDto {
  @ApiProperty()
  name: string;

  @ApiProperty()
  age: number;

  @ApiProperty()
  breed: string;
}

@ApiOkResponse({
  schema: {
    allOf: [
      { $ref: getSchemaPath(PaginatedDto) },
      {
        properties: {
          results: {
            type: 'array',
            items: { $ref: getSchemaPath(CatDto) },
          },
        },
      },
    ],
  },
})
async findAll(): Promise<PaginatedDto<CatDto>> {}
```

